Accordingly, I pass the following:
ORDER i) The appeal is allowed-in-part;
NC: 2024:KHC:14941 ii) The judgment and award dated 03.06.2023 passed in MVC.No.4162/2020 by the Court of Chief Judge, Court of Small Causes, Member, Principal MACT, Bengaluru, is modified;
iii) The claimant is entitled to the reduced compensation of Rs.8,54,300/- as against Rs.10,05,000/-
awarded by the tribunal;
United India Insurance Co Ltd vs N L Nagaraju on 15 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/20691473/
4 iv) The claimant shall not be entitled for any interest on the compensation of Rs.25,000/- awarded towards future medical expenses;
v) The entire compensation amount shall be released in favour of the claimant upon proper verification;
vi) The amount in deposit, if any, shall be transmitted to the jurisdictional tribunal;
vii) All other terms and conditions stipulated by the tribunal shall stand intact.
